# Test organization

- Put all project-owned test files under the root `tests/` directory.
- Python backend tests belong in `tests/backend/`.
- Frontend Vitest tests belong in `tests/frontend/`; mirror component/lib folders when useful.
- Keep shared fixtures and test support under `tests/`.
- Do not add tests beside production code in `frontend/src/`, `backend/`, or `src/`.
- Update imports and runner configuration when moving tests.
- Run backend tests from the repository root with `uv run pytest -q` and frontend tests from `frontend/` with `npm test`.
